-- approvals.talk: the same tenant's approval policy. Same Script Group as
-- invoices.talk, so `send review … and wait` between them is ordered by the
-- spec, not by goroutine timing.
--
-- Grants: inbox: ask (suspending, a human answers in the tenant's web UI)
--         log:   write (fire-and-forget)

script variable autoLimit = 5000 GBP

on review {ref: n, amount: a} where a <= autoLimit
  return "approved"
end review

on review {ref: n, amount: a}
  ask inbox to ask {question: "Approve invoice " & n & " for " & a & "?",
                    choices: ["approve", "reject"]}
  -- Suspends for as long as a human takes. The Host bounds that with its own
  -- deadline and fails the call ("timeout"), because an in-memory wait of
  -- days is the wrong tool (ADR 0005).
  -- ?? `ask inbox to ask`: an Operation named `ask` reads badly. A Host
  --    naming guide for Operations would help ("question", "prompt").
  match it
    when {choice: "approve"} then return "approved"
    when {choice: "reject", note: why} then return {rejected: why}
  end match
end review
